  "details": "Description\n\nAfter setting Loading Screen to \"Random\", VRChat started failing to join worlds.\n\nSymptoms:\n\nCan log in normally\n\nCan stay in current world\n\nEvery world transition fails or breaks\n\nHappens across multiple PCs\n\nLooks like API/network/risk-control issue at first\n\nThe issue was fixed immediately after changing Loading Screen back to Default.\n\nLogs contain:\n\nInventoryItem not found\n\n/inventory/random\n\nFailed to load loading screen\n\nValue cannot be null\n\nNullReference related errors\n\nIt seems the client requests a random loading screen inventory item that does not exist, then fails to handle the null response properly.\n\nReproduction\n\nSet Loading Screen to Random\n\nRestart VRChat\n\nTry joining worlds\n\nObserve join failures / transition issues\n\nAdditional Info\n\nIssue reproduced across different PCs with same account.\n\n然后把你日志里这几段一起贴：\n\n[API] [205, 404, Get, -1 https://api.vrchat.cloud/api/1/user/.../inventory/random]\n\nInventoryItem not found\n\n[LoadingScreenManager] Failed to load loading screen\n\nValue cannot be null.\n\nParameter name: key",
